 "text": "Hello! How's your day looking? You can talk to the app. Download one and you can practice following a real person. You can choose quiet mode and only see the text. It' a good workout for backchanneling too, like \"we' and \"uh.\" You can also record yourself and listen later, which is great for seeing how you sound. Lots of app options too, so a friend might not be available and online courses cost a lot of time. Stick with quiet mode and only look at the text if you worry. The key is getting used to the pace of each word. Think of it like a game. You can, and there are good Italian language apps too. Whichever you choose, it' a great way to give your speaking muscles a workout.",
